[S3] THE INTENSIVE QUANTITY  d := |grad S_W|^2 / N_p ,  N_p = 6 L^4   (L = 2,4,6,8)
  bound D1 (rigorous):  d <= 6 beta^2 = 37.5000  for ALL L and ALL phi
  L           E     N_p      E/N_p   d(z2 s=.5) d(haar mean)  d(haar max)  d/bound
      2      64      96     0.6667     9.375000     4.546284     5.612608   0.2500
      4    1024    1536     0.6667     9.375000     4.684375     4.974280   0.2500
      6    5184    7776     0.6667     9.375000     4.668748     4.810247   0.2500
      8   16384   24576     0.6667     9.375000     4.675595     4.695815   0.2500

  exact value at z2(s=0.5):  1.5 beta^2 = 9.375000 = (18/8) * (E/N_p) * beta^2
  per-link value at z2(s=0.5): 2.25 beta^2 = 14.062500 = 18 * beta^2 / 8
  -> both are ratios of INCIDENCE COUNTS: 18 = aligned plaquette-link incidences at a
     direction-1 link, 8 = per-plaquette gradient normalisation, E/N_p = 4/6. No dynamics.

[S3b] CERTIFICATE of D1.  For one link l:  g[l,a] = sum_{p incident to l} s_{p,l,a},
      s_{p,l,a} = -(beta/2) tr(lam_a X_{p,l}) ;  Cauchy-Schwarz over the <=6 plaquettes:
        |g_l|^2 <= 6 sum_p sum_a s^2 = 6 * (beta^2/4) sum_p sin^2(psi_p) <= 9 beta^2
      => sum_l |g_l|^2 <= 9 beta^2 * E = 36 beta^2 L^4  =>  d <= 36/6 * beta^2 = 6 beta^2.
  L=2: sum_l |g_l|^2 =      900.000   6*sum_p sum s^2 =     1800.000   ratio = 0.5000  (<=1 = certificate holds)
  L=4: sum_l |g_l|^2 =    14400.000   6*sum_p sum s^2 =    28800.000   ratio = 0.5000  (<=1 = certificate holds)
  L=6: sum_l |g_l|^2 =    72900.000   6*sum_p sum s^2 =   145800.000   ratio = 0.5000  (<=1 = certificate holds)
  L=8: sum_l |g_l|^2 =   230400.000   6*sum_p sum s^2 =   460800.000   ratio = 0.5000  (<=1 = certificate holds)

