[S6] HESSIAN SIDE -- FD Hessian, row-sum (Gershgorin) bound, binding eigenvector
     D2 (structural): a plaquette touches 4 links, a link sits in 6 plaquettes => bounded
     degree => max_i sum_j |Hess_ij| is O(beta) with an L-independent constant.
  L=2: lambda_min = -9.999998   lambda_max = +7.499999   max row-sum = 15.0000 = 6.0000 beta   (0.1s)
  L=4: lambda_min = -9.999998   lambda_max = +7.499999   max row-sum = 15.0000 = 6.0000 beta   (17.0s)
  => the Hessian is NOT extensive: both eigenvalues and row sums are identical at L=2,4.

  binding eigenvector structure (L=2, z2 config):
    lambda_min = -9.999998   ||v||^2 = 1.000000
